% lps-converted-from: event_calculus.lps
% This document was written from the LPS program event_calculus.lps, which says the same thing in the older syntax. The two run alike, and tools/lps_to_le_test.pl checks that they do. The first line above is what keeps the older file from being read as this document's companion, which would run every rule twice.

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 10.

the events are:
    *a thing* gives *a second thing* with *a third thing*; known as gives.
    *a thing* takes *a second thing*.
    *a thing* drops *a second thing*.
    *a thing* walks *a second thing*.

the actions are:
    none needed.

the fluents are:
    *a thing* has *a second thing*.
    the at of *a thing* is *a second thing*; known as at.

the knowledge base event_calculus includes:

initially mary has book
    and the at of mary is library
    and the at of john is library.

when a thing gives a second thing with a third thing
then it is not the case that the thing has the third thing.

when a thing gives a second thing with a third thing
then the second thing has the third thing.

when a thing takes a second thing
then the thing has the second thing.

when a thing drops a second thing
then it is not the case that the thing has the second thing.

when a thing walks a second thing
then the at of the thing that is a third thing becomes the second thing.

it must not be true that
    a thing gives a second thing with a third thing
    and it is not the case that the thing has the third thing.

it must not be true that
    a thing gives a second thing with a third thing
    and the at of the thing is a fourth thing
    and it is not the case that the at of the second thing is the fourth thing.


scenario one is:
    mary gives john with book from 2 to 3.
    john walks cafe from 4 to 5.
    john drops book from 6 to 7.
